      "id": "sol.hmmt-feb-calculus-2001-p8.hmmt",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "\\(\\sum_{n=0}^{\\infty} \\cot \\left(n^{2}+n+1\\right)=\\sum_{n=0}^{\\infty} \\arctan \\left(\\frac{1}{n^{2}+n+1}\\right)=\\sum_{n=0}^{\\infty} \\arctan (n+1)-\\arctan (n)\\) by the sum/difference formula for tangent. This sum, taken out to \\(n=N\\), telescopes to \\(-\\arctan (0)+\\arctan (N+1)\\). So as \\(N\\) goes to infinity, the sum goes to \\(\\pi / 2\\).",
